From a4875b3b4426a9b3045123fd1c8f61006073fa63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:55:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] texpacks: remember region hashes by VRAM content instead of
 decoding every texture

replace() decoded and hashed every texture region the GS created. The game
re-creates the same texture (same registers, same VRAM bytes) tens of times a
second, so ~99.9% of those decodes produced a hash already seen. The hash is
over decoded RGBA (through the palette), so it cannot be computed from raw
data; instead the hash is memoised under (layout, palette, 256-bit digest of
every GS page the decode can read). The digest is a linear pass over the
pages, ~20-60x cheaper than decode+hash; equal inputs decode to equal pixels,
so results are exact. Hash definition, dump names and replacement logic are
unchanged (decode is only deferred until a dump or a button composition needs
the pixels). The pure decode/hash/digest code moves to gs_texregion.h (no
Vulkan/raylib) so tests can drive it.

Measured (thread time inside replace(), instrumented with GA2_TEXSTATS=1):
  Zettai prebattle, 560 s, 1.04M calls: 101.1 s -> 8.0 s (97 us -> 6.7 us per call);
    game-thread CPU share 66.9% -> 51.6% of a core.
  Zettai + English pack 560 s: 93.7 s -> 11.8 s; game thread 62.7% -> 53.8%.
  Eigou 2 narration 90 s: 6.87 s / 61.7k calls (111 us) -> 0.31 s / 159k calls (1.9 us).
  Mugen 1 opening 120 s: 165k calls, 1.07 s total.
Equality: GA2_TEXCHECK=1 recomputes every memo hit: 873k hits in a Zettai run
and 46k in Eigou 2, 0 mismatches. Same replaced hashes (5 button textures in
Eigou 2; 22 in Zettai with the English pack; title label with the test mod);
Eigou 2 and Mugen 1 dump directory listings identical (44 / 26 names); Zettai
listings differ only by timing-dependent animation frames, as between two
baseline runs. New tests prove the digest covers every page a decode reads
(mutation-checked: dropping the page-spill fails them); 613 tests pass.

Switches: GA2_TEXMEMO=0 (old behaviour), GA2_TEXCHECK=1, GA2_TEXSTATS=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
